# Actors and controllers

A widget on the shell scene graph is a `GObject` subclass. Feature controllers (`TopBar`, `Dock`, `PatchSet`, `SignalTracker`) stay plain classes.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
class ClockButton {
    constructor() {
        this.actor = new St.Button();
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD
class ClockButton extends St.Button {
    static {
        GObject.registerClass(this);
    }

    _init() {
        super._init({
            style_class: 'better-gnome-shell-clock',
            label: _('Clock'),
        });
    }
}
```

Call the actor initializer `_init`, then `super._init(...)`. Do not register a feature controller with `GObject`.
